Not really a proper genoless ascension, since it wasn't planned...just 
never found any scrolls of geno.

Continuing my quest to ascend every class, I turned to ranger.  This guy 
had a bit of early luck with a couple of magic lamps, one off a bones pile.  
Decided to put the first wish towards GDSM and the second towards 
Stormy...which was kind of a bad idea, really, since wishing didn't give me 
proficiency.  Still, the extra power got me through the mines pretty quick, 
which I was already doing quite well in by clearing monsters with my bow 
and my cat.  After finishing the mines, I went down a bit in the main 
dungeon till I found an altar.  My first time down, I didn't see Sokoban, 
so I ended up skipping it.  Did the quest, which wasn't too hard, and got 
me a nice bow.  Didn't really use it that much, but it's nice to have 
around anyway.  Perseus left me a shield of reflection, and since I was 
wielding Stormy more than Diana, and I wasn't planning on using anything 
but divination spells (just ident, basically), I decided to use it.  I 
somehow managed to clear the castle without having fire resistance yet...a 
red dragon soon solved that problem.  Filled out my ascension kit...decided 
to go with gauntlets of power since I was struggling with carrying capacity 
without them.  Mapped out Gehennom the old fashioned way...walking around.  
Just did that to make sure I got all the items, since I really was hoping 
for more scrolls of charging so I could refill my magic marker which I 
carelessly let get dry.

I decided to perform some alchemy, something I usually don't do, since I 
was trying to keep my level low, and my hp were pathetically low (about 
120).  After that, it was time to storm Rodney's tower.  On the first 
floor, suddenly Demogorgon appeared.  This was actually my first encounter 
with him.  Fortunately, I had just wielded a cockatrice corpse to whack an 
Arch-lich, which may have been what summoned him.  One whack and I had a 
nice statue.  Then I whacked the stuff around him, took a few steps...and 
died of sickness.  Ooops, talk about not paying attention.  Fortunately I 
had an AoLS on.

Rodney died, I went down.  Moloch's sanctuary wasn't too bad.  Got the 
amulet, and started my way out...when a master lich summoned a bunch of 
monsters, including a MMF.  Before I could kill him, he'd sucked my brains 
several times.  This was extremely annoying, after all the work I did 
mapping.  Getting out of Gehennom took a long time, but the main dungeon 
took even longer.  Still, I was surprised by how few times Rodney showed 
up.

Exited the dungeon, and used scrolls of gold detection (confused, not 
cursed) to find the portals.  I basically rushed through the whole set of 
elemental planes as quick as I could, not stopping to fight.  Soon I was on 
astral.  Went left, to Famine.  I had to kill him more times than I like, 
but by the end he had to have been level drained about as low as he could 
get.  Altar was lawful, so I went to the middle, killing Pestilence in the 
process.  A lot of fighting later (chars that can't two-weapon don't have a 
lot of attack power to begin with, and Stormy's not really that great a 
weapon), I got to the altar, and it was Chaotic.  Forgot to blow my magic 
whistle, but oh well.  One #Offer later, and I was a demigod.

Two more classes left: Monk and Healer.  Monk will be first, since I've 
already gotten one of them to the plane of Fire (where he died an extremely 
unfortunate death).  Will probably try to keep vegetarian with the monk, 
since it seems appropriate.  On the other hand, will probably use a wish on 
the Staff of Aesculapius, since I'm not sure if I could do a weaponless 
ascension.  We'll see how things go.

